# Annotations point at parts: a brace under part of a formula, a box around a span, a cross and a check.
title "Pointing at parts"
mark f tex tex="y = \textcolor{wx}{w_1 x_1 + w_2 x_2} + \textcolor{b}{b}"
mark a array items=[3,1,4,1,5] label="inputs"
Say: "A neuron adds up |sum|weighted inputs, then a bias."
@sum mark sb brace of=f[wx] label="weighted sum"
Say: "The bias is |one|one extra number."
@one mark eb enclose of=f[b] label="bias"
Say: "Only the |mid|middle three inputs matter here."
@mid mark u underline of=a[1:3] label="these three"
